sits at the path the prose claims, and no id was reconstructed from a prefix. The five new artifacts are signed by codex 5f12e916, the actor the request was addressed to, so the authority is correct and no actor was impersonated. No secret, credential, input-validation or bounds surface is touched, and the change cannot alter kernel verification, admission or fold behaviour because it ships no code. One residual hazard, which the review request asked me to account for and which is an obligation on my own promise 8b515d0b rather than a defect in this head: the four predecessors f0cf16ee internal/intent, 940b782f internal/connector/github, 8aa25919 internal/statusview and 416d7247 ui are authored by claude and are still live, and at this head 8aa25919 is still named by ten other doc pages and 416d7247 by four. docset SucceededRetirements treats a retirement as succeeded only when the supersession itself rests on an artifact covering the same path; 85a65b32 rested on its target alone, which is precisely why 21ffa924 turned fatal rather than merely reporting. So when I discharge 8b515d0b, each of those retirements must rest on its covering successor, 6ad2e2da for internal/statusview and fd0680ef for ui in particular, or the gate goes red on fourteen pages this head does not touch. f0cf16ee and 940b782f are named by no doc page at this head and are safe either way. I record this before the merge so the obligation is legible rather than discovered afterwards.\n\nSIMPLIFICATION. Nothing to cut. This is the minimum edit that satisfies the conditions: thirteen lines of front matter, no prose churn, no baseline entry, and none of the broader docset cleanup the request explicitly forbade. Dropping the observe and telemetry anchors instead of refreshing them is itself the simplifying choice, since a page that does not describe those packages should not flare when they move. Two observations I deliberately do not raise as changes. internal/custody is named in the package-boundary table but carries no artifact anywhere in the log, so it cannot be cited yet. AGENTS.md and SKILL.md are named in that table and do have live fresh artifacts, 49aff5d6 and b6bbafc1, that are not cited; both rows are repository policy rather than behaviour this page describes, the request fixed the set at thirteen, and adding them would widen the basis without strengthening any condition. Either would be separate work under its own request.\n\nVERDICT: approved. No changes requested. The head is exactly 9be4d59a310a41f300debf048b24155b68b65f3a; any change to it invalidates this approval.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:68164843c847691633fce163891793a33d939261","head":"9be4d59a310a41f300debf048b24155b68b65f3a","verdict":"approved"}}